# Build context for the sandbox image (.devcontainer/Dockerfile, built with
# context `.` by publish-image.yml, install.sh and `pi-rukas rebuild`).
#
# `COPY . ${PI_ENSEMBLE_DIR}` ships whatever is listed here, so each entry is a
# local-only tree that the image build and the runtime never read. Everything
# install.sh and the extension need stays in: extension/, skill/, pi-prompts/,
# manifests/, agents-base/, modules/, agents.json, build.sh, install*.sh,
# bin/, docs/, .pi/worktree-setup.
#
# dist/prompts is excluded because install.sh rebuilds it inside the image
# (`PI_ENSEMBLE_BASE=$ENSEMBLE_DIR PROMPTS_DIR=$ENSEMBLE_DIR/dist/prompts
# ./build.sh standard`); a stale host build is the noise this drops, not the
# artefact roles.ts reads at runtime.

# Version control — the image's build commit comes from the GITHUB_SHA build
# arg (.pi/pi-rukas-commit), never from a checkout.
.git
.gitignore

# Driver / worktree scratch, and the run artefacts .gitignore calls local-only.
.worktrees
tmp
outputs
.pi-subagents
.feynman
.pi/lean-state
.pi/work-state

# Dependencies — installed inside the image (extension/ via bun, pi/ctx7/
# parallel-cli via npm).
**/node_modules

# Built artefacts, regenerated by install.sh in the image.
dist

# Editor / OS / local-config noise.
**/.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea
.vscode
.env
.env.local

# Operator state: permissions.json and decisions.json are per-clone local
# overrides, so a stale host copy must not become baked-in image content.
# .pi/mcp.json, work.json, verify-cmd*, worktree-setup and the rest stay —
# they are committed image content.
.pi/permissions.json
.pi/decisions.json
